    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="0892" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg788"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Woodward Electoral Mission/9:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Beaulac</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-01-02T12:00:00-05:45">January 2,
                            1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1. Department’s 227, December 31, 8 p.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d810-f1"/> I am
                    communicating the Department’s 223, December 29, 6 p.m. to President Moncada by
                    special messenger today. I am prepared to release Department’s statement for
                    publication on January 5th. I shall discuss details of the Department’s telegram
                    with President Moncada on his return to Managua next week, and shall report by
                    telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
